From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maan2003 <manmeetmann2003@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:36:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] libexpr: record what evaluation observes of local inputs;
 C API

With record-input-reads, mounted local inputs are wrapped in an accessor
that records what each read observed (BLAKE3 of contents and listings,
stat types, symlink targets), and forcing a source-info attribute such
as rev records its value. Observations are kept by the EvalState, named
by the input as evaluation named it and the path within it, and returned
by nix_eval_state_input_observations.

nix_local_input_open/observe observe a local input again through its
accessor, with the same code, so a caller can tell whether a result
still holds by comparing. The accessor hides its fingerprint and
physical path so copies are always walked through it.

nix_eval_state_builder_eval_settings_as_abstract_settings lets C API
users set evaluator settings. HashSink takes experimental-feature
settings like hashString, so observations can use BLAKE3 without
enabling blake3-hashes for user code.
